                            "A type of plant of the genus Eucharis, found in Central and South America and with white flowers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ace502de-f2bd-4ea9-86a5-3d01771c48b8",
                                "sense_id": "965eaadb-5087-308f-876a-31ff589e2031",
                                "text": "But sometimes they are gentle and soft like the dew on the lips of the eucharis Before the sun comes warm with his lover's kiss, You are sea-foam, pure with the star's loveliness, Not mortal, a flower, a fairy, too fair for the beauty-shorn earth, All wonderful things, all beautiful things, gave of their wealth to your birth: O I love you so much, not recking of passion, that I feel it is wrong, But men will love you, flower, fairy, non-mortal spirit burdened with flesh, Forever, life-long."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc8ffd62-c61d-4939-a8b3-c5961b7af999",
                                "sense_id": "965eaadb-5087-308f-876a-31ff589e2031",
                                "text": "As a cut bloom, the Christmas Rose vies with the eucharis and pancratium."
                            }
                        ]
